# Nothing rendered or regenerable is version-controlled. The MP4 is published as a
# GitHub Release asset, not committed — it is ~12 MB of binary that bloats every
# clone and cannot be learned from. The source files (.md/.html/.json/.py) ARE the
# reference build; everything below is reproduced from them, per README.md
# § "Reproducing the render".
*.mp3
*.mp4
out/
renders/
assets/

# Review artifacts: contact sheets and frame stills from the Studio round.
# `npx hyperframes preview` regenerates them from the composition.
snapshots/

# Regenerated by `npx hyperframes transcribe` and scripts/caption_gen.py.
transcript.json
voiceover.srt
voiceover.vtt
captions-review.json
captions-review.previous.json
out/final.srt
out/final.vtt
.hve/captions-state.json

# Phase scratch. `.hve/brief-state.json` IS committed — it is the consent record
# that proves each phase was approved, not a cache.
.hve/_*
